  "_note": "W14-06, filled at RC-106b (Q-W14-04 closed by the wave 14 close-out dispatch). Catalog mega-menu data (S-01): exactly the 7 top-level categories and 7 subcategories of the wave 14 audit section 1.2, RO labels verbatim and in order, RU labels translated in the site's existing vocabulary. AMENDED (W24-04): every row opens its own page. RC-130 repointed each row from a service page to its category page, and until wave 24 a SUBCATEGORY row opened its parent's page, which is finding F-03: a visitor clicking Polistiren expandat landed on the top of Sisteme de termoizolație. Each subcategory now has a real page of its own at /catalog/<parent>/<child>/, and build.js asserts that every menu href is a page this build emits and that a child's page sits under its parent's. Shape: categories[] of { label: {ro, ru}, href: {ro, ru}, children?: [ { label: {ro, ru}, href: {ro, ru} } ] }. Two levels, never three: build.js refuses a child with children, a label that is not real in both locales, and a row with no href. AMENDED (W26-06, rulings W26-R5 and W26-R7): a top-level row may carry 'listed': false, which keeps every page and data use it has and takes it off the /catalog/ index and the header Catalog panel. Acoperișuri carries it: its products live on /servicii/acoperisuri/ and its catalogue pages are redirects there. And categories[2] is labelled 'Plăci flexibile' / 'Гибкая плитка', URL unchanged: the records are flexible stone and clay sheets, not fired ceramic tile. AMENDED W27-FIX-15 (W27-R-21): `menu_position` orders the index tiles and the menu rows (1 termoizolatie, 2 Acoperisuri, 3 Garduri; the rest keep their data order after them); `menu_children: false` lists a category as one row with no sub-list; `external: true` marks a category whose href is not a catalogue page and that builds none. The roofing category is LISTED again and its parent route is a real page, the two roofing bentos and nothing else; its seven children stay redirect pages.",
